  "term": "hemoglobinopathy",
  "definition": "A hemoglobinopathy is a hereditary disorder involving hemoglobin, the blood component affected in sickle cell disease. In this context, it refers to an inherited condition that can contribute to serious pregnancy-related health risks and complications.",
